From 07d4e030a761615825d7b7833f880c14dc193626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core/desktopentry: watch application directories created
 later

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-only

The monitor skipped a desktop entry directory that did not exist at startup
and watched only the first level of subdirectories, so DesktopEntries missed
the first flatpak install (it creates exports/share/applications), the first
entry in ~/.local/share/applications and entries in a new subdirectory until
an unrelated change in a watched ancestor happened to cause a rescan.

Watch the closest existing ancestor of a missing directory and every
directory above it, watch subdirectories at any depth, and re-arm after each
change so directories created since then are watched too. A change in an
ancestor alone no longer rescans unless a desktop entry directory appeared or
disappeared with it.
---
 src/core/CMakeLists.txt                |   3 +
 src/core/desktopentrymonitor.cpp       |  92 +++++++++++++-----
 src/core/desktopentrymonitor.hpp       |   9 +-
 src/core/test-desktop-entry-monitor.py | 127 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 src/core/test-desktop-entry-monitor.py

diff --git a/src/core/CMakeLists.txt b/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
